.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.ROWS" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.rows \- HTMLTableElement: rows property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]rows\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface returns a live
\f[CR]HTMLCollection\f[R] of all \f[CR]<tr>\f[R] elements that are a
child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R] element, or a child of one of the
table\(cqs \f[CR]<thead>\f[R], \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R], and
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] children.
The members of the \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] appear first, followed by members
of the \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] and the table itself, and members of the
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] come last, sorted by tree order within each group.
.PP
Although the property is read\-only, the returned object is live and is
automatically updated when the \f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] changes.
.SH VALUE
A live \f[CR]HTMLCollection\f[R] of \f[CR]HTMLTableRowElement\f[R]
objects.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] myRows = myTable.rows;
\f[B]const\f[R] firstRow = myTable.rows[0];
\f[B]const\f[R] lastRow = myTable.rows.item(myTable.rows.length \- 1);
.EE
.PP
This demonstrates how you can use both indexed access and the
\f[CR]HTMLCollection.item()\f[R] method to obtain individual rows in the
table.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement.insertRow()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement.deleteRow()\f[R]
